 "uncertain": [
  {
   "item": "Order-of-battle depth",
   "note": "Soviet side is at corps/division/brigade level (E05, as of 19 Nov 1942). German 6th Army and Romanian armies are at corps/division level (E06), but E06 spans Sep 1942-Feb 1943: presence on 19 Nov of each German division is not confirmed by it. 4th Panzer Army: only the XLVIII Panzer Corps, 22nd Panzer and Romanian 1st Armoured (E01) are included; its other formations, the 11th Panzer, 17th Panzer, Army Detachment Hollidt and the 15th Luftwaffe Field Division are omitted (no arrival dates). Italian 8th Army: one army-level element only (corps/divisions not retrieved). Hungarian 2nd Army omitted."
  },
  {
   "item": "Omitted Soviet sub-units",
   "note": "Fortified regions, anti-tank rifle battalions, armoured-car battalions, armoured trains, air armies, the Volga Flotilla and the Stalingrad air-defence corps are listed in E05 but omitted (positions and sizes unknown; no air or naval model)."
  },
  {
   "item": "All start positions",
   "note": "Approximate sector anchors (G03); not from any positional source. Soviet bridgeheads, the Stalingrad pocket sectors and the Romanian Don front are inferred from the place names in E01/E02/E05."
  },
  {
   "item": "Air units",
   "note": "OMITTED: no sourced Luftwaffe or Soviet airfield order of battle and the airlift is an abstraction (see pool note)."
  },
  {
   "item": "Airlift / supply",
   "note": "E03: requirement 680 t/day, under 20% delivered, about 500 transports. No delivered tonnage per day, no Pitomnik data, no Volga ferry data. Modelled only by a German fuel/supply pool at 50% scale (G01) and by Tatsinskaya/Morozovsk as the only German supply sources; the pocket is cut off from them by terrain/enemy control, not by an airlift flow (engine gap, see docs/EASTERN_FRONT_RESEARCH.md)."
  },
  {
   "item": "River ice (iceFromHour 168, iceFullHour 504)",
   "note": "GAME-SCALE (G01), not sourced: ice begins on day 7 (26 Nov) and is load-bearing on day 21 (10 Dec). No thaw (iceThawHour unset) because the scenario ends in January. Needs a sourced Volga/Don freeze date to replace it."
  },
  {
   "item": "Gumrak and Pitomnik airliftTonsPerDay 68 each",
   "note": "Upper bound derived from E03 (under 20% of 680 t/day delivered); the real delivered daily tonnage and the Pitomnik field are not in the sources read. Other airfields have no airlift field (unsourced)."
  },
  {
   "item": "Soviet Volga-bank supply source (krasnoslobodsk)",
   "note": "Position from E09 (Wikipedia coordinates). Beketovka is also a Soviet supply source (game-scale). Their role as a Soviet supply source is GAME-SCALE (G01), added so the Stalingrad Front mechanised corps are not cut from supply; no ferry, tonnage or crossing facts are sourced (E02 only says the defenders were pressed against the Volga)."
  },
  {
   "item": "Rivers",
   "note": "Terrain/infra rebuilt by map-engineer with OSM rivers (Chir, Myshkova, Don, Volga, etc.); river-flag cells make the Chir a real obstacle as in Dec 1942, so movement and probe results changed from earlier runs."
  },
  {
   "item": "Gumrak/Pitomnik garrison and airlift split",
   "note": "The 60th Motorized Infantry Division (sourced OOB, E06) is anchored at Gumrak so the field is not empty at start; its position is approximate (G03) and no source places it there. Pitomnik position is from E10. Airlift cap 136 t/day (20% of 680, E03 bound) is split 68/68 between Gumrak and Pitomnik, a game-scale split."
  },
  {
   "item": "Southern Soviet supply points (svetly_yar, tinguta)",
   "note": "Positions from OSM Nominatim (E08). Their role as Soviet supply sources is GAME-SCALE (G01): the southern Stalingrad Front start area was otherwise 100+ km from any source. No railhead or depot facts are sourced."
  },
  {
   "item": "Stalingrad Front 51st/57th Army start positions",
   "note": "Moved north (to about 47.95N and 48.22N) from an earlier 47.4-47.95N placement that left 12 units more than 70 km from any Soviet supply source (permanently cut off). No source gives these positions; the new ones sit within about 20-50 km of the Tinguta/Svetly Yar supply points. Approximate (G03)."
  },
  {
   "item": "Link-up date conflict",
   "note": "E01 lead: ring closed late 22 Nov at Kalach; body: Kalach captured 22 Nov, link-up at Sovetsky about 16:00 on 23 Nov. Both are recorded as events (sg.ev.kalach, sg.ev.linkup); 23 Nov is used as the closure (more detailed)."
  },
  {
   "item": "Reinforcements",
   "note": "2nd Guards Army (ready 15 Dec), 3rd Guards Army (Little Saturn 16 Dec), LVII Panzer Corps with 6th and 23rd Panzer (12 Dec): dates from E03; arrival points are approximate; 6th Panzer is said to have unloaded at Morozovsk but is placed at the proposed Kotelnikovo jump-off."
  },
  {
   "item": "Locations",
   "note": "Coordinates from Wikipedia (E07) or OSM Nominatim (E08); Beketovka is the OSM aerodrome object (approximate); Pitomnik, Sovetsky, Nizhne-Chirskaya and Chernyshkovskaya omitted (no coordinate found). Gumrak uses the Volgograd airport position (modern)."
  },
  {
   "item": "Tatsinskaya date",
   "note": "24 Dec used for the airfield loss; E03 gives no date in the text read."
  },
  {
   "item": "Weather",
   "note": "Qualitative only (E02: temperatures tens of degrees below freezing); probabilities and temperatures are game-scale (G01). Volga/Don ice is not modelled."
  },
  {
   "item": "Nation resources / strengths / morale",
   "note": "Game-scale (G01). Romanian morale/experience set low and Soviet 45/76; E01 supports only the qualitative statements (bombardment aimed at non-German units; Romanian rout)."
  }
 ]
